body:
`reportForViewer` is meant to produce a `ReportSchema` (where `type` is the literal `'report'`), but the mapped object currently preserves the spec report's `type` (e.g. `'summary'` in `sales_performance_q1`). If any downstream code starts relying on `ReportSchema.type` (or if schema validation is added), this will be invalid. Consider explicitly setting `mapped.type = 'report'` in this boundary mapping (while preserving the spec's report-kind in a different property if needed).
```suggestion
    const mapped: any = { ...reportData };
    // Ensure the mapped object conforms to ReportSchema where type must be the literal 'report'
    mapped.type = 'report';
```

This mapping uses `any` for `mapped`, `col`, and `f`, which hides potential runtime issues (e.g., `name` becoming `undefined` if neither `col.field` nor `col.name` is present). Since this is a boundary adapter, it’s a good place to enforce a minimal shape: define a typed `SpecColumn` input, produce `ReportField[]`, and validate/filter out columns without a usable `name` (optionally logging a warning).
```suggestion
    type SpecColumn = {
      field?: string;
      name?: string;
      label?: string;
      aggregate?: string;
    };

    type ReportField = {
      name: string;
      label?: string;
      aggregation?: string;
      showInSummary?: boolean;
    };

    type ReportSection = {
      type: 'summary' | 'table';
      title?: string;
      columns?: { name: string; label?: string }[];
    };

    const mapped: {
      title?: string;
      label?: string;
      columns?: SpecColumn[];
      fields?: ReportField[];
      sections?: ReportSection[];
      // Allow additional properties from the original reportData
      [key: string]: unknown;
    } = { ...reportData };

    if (!mapped.title && typeof mapped.label === 'string') {
      mapped.title = mapped.label;
    }

    // Map spec 'columns' (field/label/aggregate) → ReportSchema 'fields' (name/label/aggregation)
    if (!mapped.fields && Array.isArray(mapped.columns)) {
      const fields: ReportField[] = [];

      mapped.columns.forEach((col, index) => {
        const name = col.field || col.name;
        if (!name) {
          // Skip columns that do not provide a usable field/name
          return;
        }

        const field: ReportField = {
          name,
          label: col.label,
        };

        if (col.aggregate) {
          field.aggregation = col.aggregate;
          field.showInSummary = true;
        }

        fields.push(field);
      });

      if (fields.length > 0) {
        mapped.fields = fields;
      }
    }

    // Auto-generate sections from fields when sections are missing
    if (!mapped.sections && Array.isArray(mapped.fields) && mapped.fields.length > 0) {
      const hasSummaryFields = mapped.fields.some((f) => f.showInSummary);
      mapped.sections = [
        ...(hasSummaryFields ? [{ type: 'summary', title: 'Key Metrics' }] : []),
        {
          type: 'table',
          title: 'Details',
          columns: mapped.fields.map((f) => ({
            name: f.name,
            label: f.label,
          })),
        },
      ];
    }
```
